// references.go is the Go binding of store.v1's reference contract (see
// store/v1/reference.proto and reference_service.proto): integrity for
// references no database foreign key can enforce, because the resource they
// name lives in another database or another service.
//
//   - On write, each reference a resource sets is proven to exist with the
//     target's standard AIP Get by name (ReferenceResolver). Missing ->
//     ErrReferenceNotFound.
//   - On delete, the resource's referrers are asked for
//     (ReferrerChecker, over store.v1.ReferenceService.ListReferrers) and each
//     referrer's (store.v1.reference).on_delete applies: RESTRICT refuses
//     (ErrReferenced), ALLOW lets it go, NOTIFY lets it go and publishes a
//     CloudEvent (EventTypeReferenceDeleted).
//   - On purge, a row anything still refers to is kept, never failed and
//     never cascaded through.
//   - A reconciler re-runs the Get for every stored reference and reports the
//     dangling ones.
//
// The generated repositories call all of it from above the database, so the
// GORM and GraphQL adapters enforce it alike. Within one physical database a
// real foreign key does the work instead, and its violations surface as
// ErrForeignKey.

